<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">YORKVILLE INTERNATIONAL CAPITAL CORP.</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO UNAUDITED CONDENSED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">JUNE&#160;30, 2026</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_-Zb5E5eFE0KYMYqEs_PhBw_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The key measures of segment profit or loss reviewed by the CODM are income earned on the Trust Account and formation, general and administrative expenses. The CODM reviews income earned on the Trust Account to measure and monitor shareholder value and determine the most effective strategy of investment with the Trust Account funds. Formation, general and administrative expenses are reviewed and monitored by the CODM to manage and forecast cash to ensure enough capital is available to complete a Business Combination or similar transaction within the Combination Period. The CODM also reviews formation, general and administrative expenses to manage, maintain and enforce all contractual agreements to ensure costs are aligned with all agreements and budget. Formation, general and administrative expenses, as reported on the statements of operations, are the significant segment expenses provided to the CODM on a regular basis.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">All other segment items included in net income are reported on the statements of operations and described within their respective disclosures.</p></ix:continuation><a id="Tc_sBwBc0eyCU2mgxlhaU8bTQ_1_2"></a><a id="Tc_I4zF8pzxxES3tfHeo-N2vg_2_2"></a><a id="Tc_HYM6QDLFr0KhbwWqXtisdg_3_0"></a><a id="Tc_YSC1WgtuekmLb19JgO0WWQ_3_2"></a><a id="Tc_GqPd13vF00WQu7WPfleAOA_4_0"></a><a id="Tc_Z6kP5O4LfE2ZiW73pJEiDw_4_2"></a><a id="Tc_GNc35ETtSE6ayFtHrv53Rg_5_0"></a><a id="Tc_G-8iKsaVnEaTFpRaIMJhNA_5_4"></a><a id="Tc_g6AERFqZNUmLlj_KeZZbiw_6_0"></a><a id="Tc_HJkbbWbzo0yRqrW7_pa16g_6_4"></a><a id="Tc_r0MNtKQXu0KBD8GLSoqDDQ_7_0"></a><a id="Tc_pYhz2nMBOk6KMv3NBbCQ7w_8_0"></a><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_ZIduQ53RtUGpPMW0jZI-Pg" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionsDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_8nw7X09yo0qd1AAf7dVsPA" continuedAt="Tb_8nw7X09yo0qd1AAf7dVsPA_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Note&#160;6&#160;&#8212;&#160;Related Party Transactions</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Founder Shares</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On April&#160;2, 2026, the Company issued an aggregate <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_jypfYu4bSUK4FLFXNmez7w" contextRef="Duration_4_2_2026_To_4_2_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_8UpRaK0KHkSIp9nxdyNbug" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodSharesNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_90L39-dzl0mEzP3uNamJtw">15,333,333</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;B ordinary shares, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_C_8k089Vlk-_3c1ur5CRMQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_2_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_XI1kxqY0X0m1a9zG3Q0_JA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_oX0nb-V2006G1fPOlyFiuQ">0.0001</ix:nonFraction> par value (the &#8220;Founder Shares&#8221;), in exchange for a $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_4_2_2026_To_4_2_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_8UpRaK0KHkSIp9nxdyNbug" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:StockIssuedDuringPeriodValueNewIssues" scale="0" id="Narr_bWucojsGS0aJwVx2uC4_nQ">25,000</ix:nonFraction> payment (approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_C_8k089Vlk-_3c1ur5CRMQ" contextRef="As_Of_4_2_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_XI1kxqY0X0m1a9zG3Q0_JA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:SharesIssuedPricePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_1iK9emsGGUKSycco9C0flA">0.002</ix:nonFraction> per share) from the Sponsor to cover certain expenses on behalf of the Company.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In conjunction with the closing of the Initial Public Offering, the Sponsor granted membership interests to each of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_director_1Cv3rj-uEUOp_1FyV4gwWA" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_gMHXhYSZlEqZu2dAFYozTQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yicc:NumberOfIndependentDirectors" scale="0" id="Narr_Fiv2Yq4RvUOPGHPWF1Etkg">three</ix:nonFraction> independent directors of the Company and the Chief Executive Officer (&#8220;CEO&#8221;). The membership interests received in the Sponsor correspond to an aggregate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_jypfYu4bSUK4FLFXNmez7w" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember__cGmQYlCVEC2T1uknahTNA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yicc:MembershipInterestsSharesAvailableForDistribution" scale="0" id="Narr_NIdLLFqpikqtALf5zxM9vw">450,000</ix:nonFraction> Founder Shares, to be distributed to the directors and CEO upon consummation of a Business Combination. Each Founder Share will automatically convert to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_TSVnDiCgPkWzU1R4RmIFkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_gMHXhYSZlEqZu2dAFYozTQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yicc:CommonStockConvertibleConversionRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_LaXpOImZYEuZXshPDgTZ7A">one</ix:nonFraction> Class&#160;A ordinary share concurrently with or immediately following the consummation of a Business Combination. The Sponsor will retain all voting and dispositive power over all Founder Shares until the consummation of the Business Combination, after which the Sponsor will distribute to each holder of the membership interests its share of the Founder Shares, subject to applicable lock-up restrictions.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The sale of the membership interests to the Company&#8217;s directors is in the scope of FASB ASC Topic 718, &#8220;Compensation-Stock Compensation&#8221; (&#8220;FASB ASC 718&#8221;). Under FASB ASC 718, stock-based compensation associated with equity-classified awards is measured at fair value