;">The membership interests related to the Founder Shares were granted subject to a performance condition (i.e., the occurrence of a Business Combination). Compensation expense related to the Founder Shares is recognized only when the performance condition is probable of occurrence under the applicable accounting literature in this circumstance. As of June&#160;17, 2026, the Company determined that a Business Combination is not considered probable, and, therefore, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_mzqHSp00CEKyqN0aw_p1HQ" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:AllocatedShareBasedCompensationExpense" scale="0" id="Narr_CD_mcFbptU-GqWJl77gJYg">no</ix:nonFraction> stock-based compensation expense has been recognized related to these <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_jypfYu4bSUK4FLFXNmez7w" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassBMember_mzqHSp00CEKyqN0aw_p1HQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsGrantsInPeriod" scale="0" id="Narr_QnokYcr1g0uFW0G5XHWMLQ">450,000</ix:nonFraction> Founder Shares. Stock-based compensation would be recognized at the date a Business Combination is considered probable (i.e., upon consummation of a Business Combination) in an amount equal to the number of Founder Shares multiplied by the grant date fair value per share (unless subsequently modified).</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">18</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">YORKVILLE INTERNATIONAL CAPITAL CORP.</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO UNAUDITED CONDENSED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">JUNE&#160;30, 2026</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_8nw7X09yo0qd1AAf7dVsPA_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_8nw7X09yo0qd1AAf7dVsPA_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Founder Shares are designated as Class&#160;B ordinary shares and, except as described below, are identical to the Class&#160;A Ordinary Shares included in the&#160;units sold in the initial public offering, and holders of founder shares have the same shareholder rights as Public Shareholders, except that (i)&#160;the founder shares are subject to certain transfer restrictions, as described in more detail below, (ii)&#160;the founder shares are entitled to registration rights; (iii)&#160;the Sponsor and the Company&#8217;s officers and directors entered into a letter agreement with us, pursuant to which they agree to (A)&#160;waive their redemption rights with respect to their founder shares, private placement shares and any public shares held by them in connection with the completion of the initial Business Combination, (B)&#160;waive their redemption rights with respect to their founder shares, private placement shares and any public shares held by them in connection with a shareholder vote to approve an amendment to our amended and restated memorandum and articles of association (A)&#160;to modify the substance or timing of our obligation to allow redemption in connection with our initial business combination or to redeem <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_TSVnDiCgPkWzU1R4RmIFkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_gMHXhYSZlEqZu2dAFYozTQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yicc:PublicSharesSubjectToMandatoryRedemptionPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_xlf0MbN5_EOGmBncay8ozw">100</ix:nonFraction>% of the public shares if we have not consummated an initial business combination within the Combination Period or (B)&#160;with respect to any other material provisions relating to shareholders&#8217; rights or pre-initial business combination activity, (C)&#160;waive their rights to liquidating distributions from the trust account with respect to their founder shares or private placement shares if we fail to complete the initial Business Combination within the Combination Period, although they will be entitled to liquidating distributions from the Trust Account with respect to any public shares they hold if the Company fails to complete the initial Business Combination within such time period and to liquidating distributions from assets outside the trust account and (D)&#160;vote any founder shares and private placement shares held by them and any public shares purchased during or after the initial public offering (including in open market and privately-negotiated transactions, aside from shares they may purchase in compliance with the requirements of Rule&#160;14e-5 under the Exchange Act, which would not be voted in favor of approving the Business Combination transaction) in favor of the initial Business Combination, (iv)&#160;the founder shares are automatically convertible into Class&#160;A Ordinary Shares in connection with the consummation of the initial Business Combination or earlier at the option of the holder on a <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_TSVnDiCgPkWzU1R4RmIFkw" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_gMHXhYSZlEqZu2dAFYozTQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yicc:CommonStockConvertibleConversionRatio" scale="0" id="Narr_q1CtzYva-0ivsVnAiKPoqQ">one</ix:nonFraction>-for-one basis, subject to adjustment as described herein and in the Company amended and restated memorandum and articles of association, and (v)&#160;prior to the closing of the initial Business Combination, only holders of the Class&#160;B ordinary shares will be entitled to vote on the appointment and removal of directors or continuing the Company in a jurisdiction outside the Cayman Islands (including any special resolution required to amend our constitutional documents or to adopt new constitutional documents, in each case, as a result of our approving a transfer by way of continuation in a jurisdiction outside the Cayman Islands).</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Sponsor has agreed not to transfer, assign or sell any of its Founder Shares until the earlier to occur of (A)&#160;<span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_8u2HOIhGlUiMs-DyrRuXUQ;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">six&#160;months</span></span> after the completion of the initial Business Combination or (B)&#160;subsequent to the initial Business Combination (x)&#160;if the last reported sale price of the Class&#160;A Ordinary Shares equals or exceeds $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_C_8k089Vlk-_3c1ur5CRMQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_us-gaap_StatementClassOfStockAxis_us-gaap_CommonClassAMember_ysYBCTz5hE-qyW-z5qLvbg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yicc:LockUpReleasePriceTrigger" scale="0" id="Narr_VTVt69IHVUaA_n0Rno5Wpg">12.00</ix:nonFraction> per share (as adjusted for share sub-divisions, share capitalizations, reorganizations, recapitalizations and the like) for any <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_25NK8M309E-vuGxa834ZqQ;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">20</span></span>&#160;trading&#160;days within any <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_GvHtB7KN-U6j4-dykpVr9Q;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">30</span></span>-trading&#160;day period commencing at least <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_FounderShares1Member_h4c_7Onznk-1QX1YfmuuDA" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="yicc:LockUpReleaseCommencementPeriodDays" id="Narr_iExHda2P1kaUQr1eZn2Y_Q">150&#160;days</ix:nonNumeric> after the initial Business Combination or (y)&#160;the date on which the Company completes a liquidation, merger, share exchange, reorganization or other similar transaction that results in all of the Public Shareholders having the right to exchange their ordinary shares for cash, securities or other property.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Promissory Note&#160;&#8212;&#160;Related Party</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company and the Sponsor entered into a loan agreement, whereby the Sponsor agreed to loan the Company an aggregate of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_PromissoryNoteMember_fhudKJm-R024O_VyvjbLzw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_ff8puTktREq_JwF46140BA">300,000</ix:nonFraction> to cover expenses related to the Initial Public Offering pursuant to a promissory note (the &#8220;Promissory Note&#8221;). The Promissory Note&#160;was non-interest bearing, unsecured and due at the earlier of December&#160;31, 2026 or the date on which the Company consummates the Initial Public Offering. As of June&#160;17, 2026, the Company borrowed $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_PromissoryNoteMember_nVMfyoc600Wd_sT53D0dvQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ProceedsFromNotesPayable" scale="0" id="Narr_hSspZpbxjk6_hmcvFpoJJQ">191,602</ix:nonFraction> under the Note. In connection with the consummation of the Initial Public Offering and private placement on June&#160;17, 2026, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_PromissoryNoteMember_nVMfyoc600Wd_sT53D0dvQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RepaymentsOfNotesPayable" scale="0" id="Narr_Zd4lVJJSS0ikmPDIqIIscA">191,602</ix:nonFraction> of proceeds were used to repay the Promissory Note&#160;in full. Borrowings under the note are no longer available subsequent to the consummation of the Initial Public Offering.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Administrative Services Agreement</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company entered into an agreement, commencing on the effective date of the Initial Public Offering through the earlier of the Company&#8217;s consummation of a Business Combination and its liquidation, to pay an affiliate the Sponsor a total of up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_AdministrativeServicesAgreementMember_xA0BT9ZeA0yI3WglnKk6_Q" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yicc:RelatedPartyTransactionServiceFee" scale="0" id="Narr_-382z8s55Ea8Z7sm4qhoYg">15,000</ix:nonFraction> per&#160;month for office space, utilities and secretarial and administrative support. These&#160;monthly fees will cease upon the completion of the initial Business Combination or the liquidation of the Company.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">19</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">YORKVILLE INTERNATIONAL CAPITAL CORP.</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO UNAUDITED CONDENSED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">JUNE&#160;30, 2026</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_8nw7X09yo0qd1AAf7dVsPA_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June&#160;30, 2026, there was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_AdministrativeServicesAgreementMember_A-fSXrLbqkerti5gsiLYmw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="0" id="Narr_xHiOYCITGECwXCN2NlZCXA">8,000</ix:nonFraction> in due to related party related to the agreement. The Company incurred $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_AdministrativeServicesAgreementMember_KtAepk_bxkaBFUp-IqFRUg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionAmountsOfTransaction" scale="0" id="Narr_0ywJG1zSZ0mxjUqSWy74Kg">8,000</ix:nonFraction> for the three&#160;months ended June&#160;30, 2026 and for period from March&#160;31, 2026 (inception) through June&#160;30, 2026. Amounts have been included in formation, general and administrative expenses in the accompanying statements of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">CEO Agreement</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Commencing on the consummation of the Initial Public Offering, the Company entered into an agreement with Kevin McGurn to pay an aggregate of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_CeoAgreementMember_iKNnJTlpDkabxHsvvd0IUw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yicc:RelatedPartyTransactionServiceFee" scale="0" id="Narr_ut1aZdOlgU6P-faxlx85UQ">15,000</ix:nonFraction> per&#160;month for his services as Chief Executive Officer.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of June&#160;30, 2026, there was $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_CeoAgreementMember_DvBrROcegE-PPiW3L-DNbQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="0" id="Narr_D90lLDuI10KDn1R_z6aDBw">7,000</ix:nonFraction> in due to related party related to the agreement. The Company incurred $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_CeoAgreementMember_LNkdF6xOdEK33CeJ0QXQZw" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:RelatedPartyTransactionAmountsOfTransaction" scale="0" id="Narr_yu4SPaCM_Em9uHlDVXUQAA">7,000</ix:nonFraction> for the three&#160;months ended June&#160;30, 2026 and for period from March&#160;31, 2026 (inception) through June&#160;30, 2026. Amounts have been included in formation, general and administrative expenses in the accompanying statements of operations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Related Party Loans</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">In addition, in order to fund working capital and to finance transaction costs in connection with a Business Combination, the Sponsor or an affiliate of the Sponsor or certain of our officers and directors may, but are not obligated to, loan the Company funds as may be required (the &#8220;Working Capital Loans&#8221;). If the Company completes a Business Combination, the Company would repay the Working Capital Loans. In the event that a Business Combination does not close, the Company may use a portion of the working capital held outside the Trust Account to repay the Working Capital Loans but no proceeds from the Trust Account would be used to repay the Working Capital Loans. Up to $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_WorkingCapitalLoansMember_V9a_vDRktECn-YiACINkLA" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtConversionOriginalDebtAmount1" scale="0" id="Narr_goABx3dGEU-Dr3dginZoYA">1,500,000</ix:nonFraction> of such Working Capital Loans may be convertible into private placement&#160;units of the post-Business Combination entity at a price of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_C_8k089Vlk-_3c1ur5CRMQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_WorkingCapitalLoansMember_4VV_YOEGkUux7ITucJQ2SA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="Narr_8emv1tCtBki83u5YpKvVkw">10.00</ix:nonFraction> per unit at the option of the lender. As of June&#160;30, 2026, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_lxK76_Z0YESGsS0SzcKfow" contextRef="As_Of_6_30_2026_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionAxis_yicc_WorkingCapitalLoansMember_4VV_YOEGkUux7ITucJQ2SA" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:ShortTermBorrowings" scale="0" id="Narr_hrnI0PaEIUCE3obGT51M4Q">no</ix:nonFraction> such Working Capital Loans were outstanding.</p></ix:continuation><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_ZIduQ53RtUGpPMW0jZI-Pg" name="us-gaap:CommitmentsAndContingenciesDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_spQ8jXAo50GjQrjCzFvYJg" continuedAt="Tb_spQ8jXAo50GjQrjCzFvYJg_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Note&#160;7&#160;&#8212;&#160;Commitments and Contingencies</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Registration Rights</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The holders of the Founder Shares, Private Placement Warrants and warrants that may be issued upon conversion of Working Capital Loans (and any ordinary shares issuable upon the exercise of the Private Placement Warrants or warrants issued upon conversion of the Working Capital Loans and upon conversion of the Founder Shares) will be entitled to registration rights pursuant to a registration rights agreement to be signed prior to or on the effective date of Initial Public Offering requiring the Company to register such securities for resale (in the case of the Founder Shares, only after conversion to Class&#160;A Ordinary Shares).The holders of these securities will be entitled to make up to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_item_TkrDQ-nv_kuZNRZ6eXnLng" contextRef="Duration_3_31_2026_To_6_30_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_eAFu5uUfCEKjrQLceAaghg" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yicc:MaximumNumberOfDemandsExcludingShortFormRegistrationDemandsEntitledBySecurityHolders" scale="0" id="Narr_PAUFAMkEj0GAAvi-Iz3PUA">three</ix:nonFraction> demands, excluding short form registration demands, that the Company register such securities. In addition, the holders have certain &#8220;piggy-back&#8221; registration rights with respect to registration statements filed subsequent to completion of a Business Combination and rights to require the Company to register for resale such securities pursuant to Rule&#160;415 under the Securities Act. However, the registration rights agreement provides that the Company will not be required to effect or permit any registration or cause any registration statement to become effective until the securities covered thereby are released from their lock-up restrictions. The Company will bear the expenses incurred in connection with the filing of any such registration statements.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Underwriting Agreement</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company granted the underwriters a <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_6_17_2026_To_6_17_2026_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_OverAllotmentOptionMember_FkkJQnKd1E-iOqqhuwF0wA" format="ixt-sec:durday" name="yicc:UnderwritersOverAllotmentOptionPeriod" id="Narr_y2pYen266EWu-I3g-X1MUA">45</ix:nonNumeric>-day option from the date of the Initial Public Offering to purchase an additional <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_jypfYu4bSUK4FLFXNmez7w" contextRef="As_Of_6_17_2026_us-gaap_SubsidiarySaleOfStockAxis_us-gaap_OverAllotmentOptionMember_YhCDb